{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvKRz5ZVZsGkYqA761Be","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, that's expected. `this.queue()` doesn't run your callback inside the request that queued it. It saves the callback's method name and a JSON-serializable payload to the Agent's SQLite storage, then runs it later from the queue loop. That can happen after the original request has finished, or even after the Durable Object has hibernated and woken up again. So inside the callback, `getCurrentAgent()` gives you the agent, but `request` (and usually `connection`) is `undefined`. A live `Request` object can't be saved to storage anyway.\n\nThe fix is to copy what you need from the request into the payload when you queue it, for example `this.queue(\"process\", { userId, url: request.url, authHeader })`, and read it from the payload in the callback. Don't store secrets in the payload unless you're comfortable having them saved in the Agent's storage.\n\nI answered from how the Agents SDK works, not from your code or the installed `agents` 0.27.0 source. If the callback can't see the agent itself either, that's a different problem and worth looking into."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10079,"cache_read_input_tokens":15764,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10079},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"22be5c9a-3422-41d3-a370-0a1150808f80","uuid":"8f5080b6-1ce2-40ef-b964-607340772d29","timestamp":"2026-10-11T10:48:44.683Z","request_id":"req_011CfvKRykxCfqWpcT6ZoB63"}
